From: apex project <apex@local>
Subject: [PATCH] apex: fix USB tethering disconnect panic

Add NULL check for udc/driver in usb_gadget_disconnect to prevent panic
on disconnect when UDC is already torn down.

Signed-off-by: apex project
diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/core.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/core.c
index 4c27f8da1..1f36bb2ca 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/core.c
@@ -733,7 +733,10 @@ int usb_gadget_disconnect(struct usb_gadget *gadget)
 	ret = gadget->ops->pullup(gadget, 0);
 	if (!ret) {
 		gadget->connected = 0;
-		gadget->udc->driver->disconnect(gadget);
+		if (gadget->udc && gadget->udc->driver)
+			gadget->udc->driver->disconnect(gadget);
+		else
+			pr_debug_ratelimited("usb_gadget_disconnect: udc or driver is NULL\n");
 	}
 
 out:
